<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<PermissionSet xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        PermissionSet.Description is capped at 255 characters. The full rationale below is
        security-relevant and was moved here rather than deleted; a comment is repo-only and
        is never sent to the Metadata API, so it can be as long as it needs to be. Do not
        paste this back into <description> verbatim - trim it if it needs to change there.

        Investor Relations persona: Create/Read/Edit (no Delete) on the IR-record-type
        Lead/Contact/Account population only. Deliberately NO viewAllRecords/modifyAllRecords
        - record visibility beyond owned rows comes from the Lead_IR_Investor /
        Account_Investor_Entity sharing rules (Task 11), never from this permission set.
        Record type visibility is scoped to Lead.IR_Investor / Contact.Investor /
        Account.Investor_Entity only, so an IR user cannot create or see a broker-typed row.
        Carries no broker field and no acquisitions Lead deal-screening field.

        =====================================================================
        ADDED 2026-08-16 - Offering__c, user directive (FSD Gap Tranche 1, Q1.2 follow-up).
        =====================================================================
        The design gate for FSD Tranche 1 flagged that OfferingService.ensureOnPsaExecuted
        leaves every new Offering__c row invisible to IR (Private OWD, zero sharing rules, and
        neither DPEG_IR_Edit nor DPEG_IR_View carried the object at all). The user's explicit
        instruction was: "They will be visible to IR team, right now give them read/write
        permission" - not a Gate-1 option letter, a directive. This set therefore gains
        allowRead=true, allowEdit=true on Offering__c and EDITABLE FLS on its three fields.

        allowCreate and allowDelete are DELIBERATELY false. The shell is created by
        OfferingService (system mode, off the ContractExecutionService PSA-execution path); the
        user asked for read/write on the record, not the ability to mint or remove one, and
        granting Create here would let IR bypass the one-shell-per-Opportunity idempotency the
        service enforces via OfferingSelector.selectByOpportunityIds.

        NO viewAllRecords/modifyAllRecords, matching every other grant on this set - see
        Offering__c.sharingRules-meta.xml (Offering_IR_Visibility, Edit, owner-based from
        roleAndSubordinates Acquisitions_Analyst) for how IR actually reaches a row it does not
        own. New Offerings are owned by whichever acquisitions persona executed the PSA, never
        by IR, which is exactly why record access must come from that sharing rule rather than
        from viewAllRecords on this set.

        Reconciled against usman-dpeg via sf project retrieve (2026-08-16) before this edit:
        the live set carried NO Offering__c objectPermissions or fieldPermissions entries at
        all, matching the repo file, so this is a pure addition with nothing org-side at risk
        of being replaced.
    -->
